= Communication
- Inevitable:  one cannot *not* communicate
- Episodic: Like dancing communication is fluid and continuous.
- Constructed: Communications is both verbal & non-verbal symbols and signs
- Contextual: interpretation of communication is influenced by multiple contexts

== The Lasswel formula

$ #[`who`] to underbrace(#[`what`],#[`channel`]) to #[`whom`] to #[`effect`] $

== Levels of influence
- Macro: Media systems
- Meso: Media organizations
- Micro: Media users
- One-to-Many: mass communication, public audience
- Many-to-many: group communication
- One-to-one: Interpersonal communication
- In your head: intrapersonal communication

== Message production
Speaking *always* requires intention

- _Conceptualization_ stage: The message exists as semantic and pragmatic features but not yet as words (You decide what you want to say.)
- _Formulation_ stage: The idea gets matched to lemmas (words with meaning and grammatical info, but not yet sound)
- _Phonological encoding_ stage: Actual sound and grammatical structure
- Actual _articulation_: The motor system takes over: muscles (tongue, lips, vocal cords) activate and you actually speak.

